 ## Purpose
 
-Define one provider-neutral boundary for browser-local meeting capture, a Recall.ai fallback, deferred Zoom RTMS, and artifact import without granting any provider meeting, transcript, ACL, retention, or run authority.
+Turn hosted, externally joined, locally captured, and calendar-recognized meetings into trustworthy Product-Suite meeting summaries and review-gated action candidates without collapsing four different product paths into one adapter or granting providers task/run authority.
 
 ## Success criteria
 
-- A small contract distinguishes external capture from `RoomProvider` and `RealtimeAgentAdapter`.
-- Every start is capability-, policy-, consent-, region-, ACL-, and budget-checked.
-- Canonical events are provenance-rich and idempotent; partial/outage states remain explicit.
-- Local is the bounded MVP, Recall is an explicit fallback, Zoom RTMS remains deferred behind objective exit criteria.
-- Provider deletion and Product-Suite retention are independently observable.
+- Four explicit boundaries: `RoomProvider`, `ExternalMeetingConnector`, `LocalCaptureSource`, and `MeetingRecognition`/orchestration.
+- All sources converge through canonical meeting evidence with provenance, completeness, media topology, and speaker confidence.
+- Local capture is the bounded MVP; Recall is an explicit external-join fallback; Zoom RTMS is capability-gated and deferred.
+- Google Meet and Teams platform constraints degrade capabilities explicitly rather than leaking provider assumptions into the contract.
+- Meeting-owned summaries/action candidates converge on one compact review pack; task creation requires explicit `Add` and is never automatic.
+- Consent/indicator, ACL, retention/deletion/region, retry/idempotency/outage, and cost budgets fail closed.
 
 ## Out of scope
 
-Room hosting, participant-token minting, realtime agent turns/tools, provider-owned transcripts/runs, automatic fallback without renewed disclosure, Zoom RTMS implementation, browser extension/desktop system-audio implementation, and local crash/network durability owned by sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a`.
+The LiveKit-versus-Cloudflare-RealtimeKit `RoomProvider` choice; realtime agent turns/tools; automatic recording from a calendar event; guaranteed identity from mixed-audio diarization; provider-authored canonical summaries/tasks/runs; Google Meet Media production integration while in Developer Preview; Teams compliance-recording infrastructure; Zoom RTMS implementation; and local durability owned by sibling issue `d88d461a-c259-4dc6-a751-f2b3c6898b7a`.
 
-## Selected approach
+## Approach selected
 
-Add a versioned contract with seven operations: `negotiate`, `prepare`, `start`, `stop`, `importArtifact`, `status`, and `delete`. The meeting service remains the orchestration and authority layer. Adapters translate provider/local events to canonical connector envelopes; downstream transcription and agent execution consume canonical artifacts only.
+Keep four source-specific boundaries and add a small common `MeetingEvidenceEnvelope` at the Product-Suite meeting authority. Local capture produces the first MVP evidence. Recall participates in externally hosted Zoom/Meet/Teams calls only after explicit fallback selection. Calendar recognition associates and preflights meetings but never authorizes capture. RoomProvider continues to own hosted rooms separately.
 
-The selection order is policy, not hidden failover: local when requested capabilities and consent UX are available; Recall only after explicit fallback choice and cost/region preflight; import for an existing artifact; Zoom returns a deferred capability until its exit criteria pass.
+Canonical transcript segments carry speaker label kind and confidence. Product-Suite derives meeting-owned summary and action candidates with evidence references and completeness flags. Every path renders the same compact review pack: each card shows a plain title, one-line reason/source, recommended next step, and `Add`, `Adjust`, or `Dismiss`. `Adjust` opens inline agent conversation with no more than two or three natural-language planning choices and stores the revision as a new candidate version. Structured fields/provenance remain hidden until relevant. Only authorized `Add` can idempotently promote that exact candidate version into the task system.
 
 ## Constraints and invariants
 
-- Server context derives tenant/actor; provider fields cannot select authorization scope.
-- `start` requires consent evidence and an active visible indicator; revocation stops capture.
-- Same idempotency key plus different semantics is a conflict, never a second session.
-- Webhooks are acknowledged quickly and handled asynchronously with dedupe/backoff.
-- Exact region and hard budget are negotiated inputs; unsupported means deny.
-- Product-Suite retention/deletion policy applies even when provider deletion is pending.
-- Gaps, interruptions, and incomplete deletion are durable states, not success.
+- One adapter cannot claim all four paths; source capabilities remain explicit.
+- Server context derives tenant/actor; provider/calendar/speaker metadata is never authorization.
+- Consent evidence and visible recording state are mandatory at capture/join time.
+- Low-confidence speaker identity cannot silently become an action owner.
+- Same idempotency key plus different semantics is a conflict.
+- Exact region, retention, availability, diarization mode/latency, and budget are negotiated facts.
+- Fallback changes require renewed confirmation; incomplete evidence remains incomplete.
+- Provider output cannot directly create meetings, transcripts, tasks, proposals, or runs; neither candidate generation nor adjustment creates a work item.
 
 ## Edge cases
 
-Permission denied after preflight; local source ends mid-meeting; indicator process crashes; bot pool exhaustion; duplicate/out-of-order webhook; provider reconnect changes stream identity; webhook outage exceeds provider retry window; transcript arrives before audio metadata; deletion confirmation never arrives; region changes between prepare/start; monthly budget is consumed concurrently; imported artifact hash collides with different provenance.
+Shared conference-room microphone; overlapping/similar voices; Teams speaker attribution disabled; Google Meet Media preview/ineligible participant; Recall bot denied or pool exhausted; Zoom RTMS entitlement/concurrency unavailable; calendar event moved or duplicate join URLs; local capture source ends; transcript gaps; action owner mentioned by an uncertain speaker; repeated adjustment or stale candidate version; more than three agent choices; dismissal; duplicate promotion; deletion remains pending; budget consumed concurrently.
 
 ## Ambiguity policy
 
-Choose the privacy-preserving, lower-cost, non-recording outcome. Do not broaden media, switch provider, or extend retention without explicit policy and user confirmation. Unknown provider state maps to `degraded` or `incomplete`, never `complete`.
